Package: hd-kernel-vm
Version: @META_DEB_VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: linux-image-@RELEASE@ (= @KERNEL_DEB_VERSION@),
 zfs-modules-@RELEASE@ (= @ZFS_DEB_VERSION@)
Conflicts: hd-kernel, hd-kernel-server, hd-kernel-desktop, linux-image-amd64, linux-headers-amd64,
 linux-base-amd64
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian kernel for KVM virtual machines
 Depends on the most recent HyprDebian kernel for vms of @SUITE@ and its ZFS
 module, so that they are installed and upgraded with it. The kernel is that
 of hd-kernel, linux @KERNEL_VERSION@ of Debian with its patches and its
 config, but without the drivers of hardware that a KVM vm does not have; the
 ZFS module is that of zfs-linux @ZFS_VERSION@, built against it. Both are
 built on the build server and signed with a key that is made for the build
 and thrown away, so a system needs neither DKMS nor a compiler for ZFS, and
 the kernel trusts no other key for its modules.
 .
 It replaces the kernel of Debian and the other HyprDebian kernels: installing
 it removes hd-kernel, hd-kernel-server, hd-kernel-desktop, linux-image-amd64,
 linux-headers-amd64 and linux-base-amd64.
 See hd-kernel-vm(7).
